  "draft": "Expanding $\\sin^7 x$ using complex exponentials: $\\sin x = \\frac{e^{ix} - e^{-ix}}{2i}$. Raising to the 7th power, $\\sin^7 x = \\left(\\frac{e^{ix} - e^{-ix}}{2i}\\right)^7$. Using the binomial theorem, this becomes $\\frac{1}{(2i)^7} \\sum_{k=0}^{7} \\binom{7}{k} (-1)^k e^{i(7 - 2k)x}$. Simplifying, we find that only odd powers of $e^{ix}$ contribute to $\\sin x$ terms. After collecting terms, the coefficient of $\\sin x$ corresponds to the constant $d$. By calculating the sum of coefficients for $\\sin x$, we determine that $d = \\frac{7}{128}$."
